~ # defines a node. inside a definition:
~   ||a, b, c||   captures parameters
~   ::name::      interpolates a captured parameter
~   ...           marks where the invocation body will render

#chapter ||number, title, subtitle||
@h2 ::number:: — ::title:: h2@
@p @em ::subtitle:: em@ p@
...
chapter#

~ used like this — the pipes fill the captures, the body fills the ...

@chapter
|number I|
|title The Keeper|
|subtitle On the nature of attention|
For eleven days the lamp had burned untended.
chapter@

~ captured parameters can also thread into child nodes invisibly —
~ here label, value and target flow straight into core-vocab elements.

#metric ||label, value, target||
@figure
@figcaption ::label:: figcaption@
@strong ::value:: strong@ — target ::target::
figure@
metric#

@metric |label Uptime| |value 99.2%| |target 99.5%| metric@
